                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " And he said, “The kingdom of God is as if a man should scatter seed upon the ground, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MRK.4.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MRK.4.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MRK 4:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and should sleep and rise night and day, and the seed should sprout and grow, he knows not how. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MRK.4.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MRK.4.27"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "28",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MRK 4:28"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "28",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The earth produces of itself, first the blade, then the ear, then the full grain in the ear. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MRK.4.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MRK.4.28"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "29",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MRK 4:29"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "29",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But when the grain is ripe, at once he puts in the sickle, because the harvest has come.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MRK.4.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MRK.4.29"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
